{"caveats":[],"characterization":[{"entity_id":"char_bddcd1b989f4e977","evidence_ids":["ev_f5b4a7971cccd26b"],"output":null,"settings":{},"technique":"EIS"}],"evidence":[{"char_end":216,"char_start":87,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b90ef0af6adf686c","document_char_end":66220,"document_char_start":66091,"evidence_id":"ev_f5b4a7971cccd26b","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The EIS measurements were conducted in the potential range of 1.3–1.7 V versus RHE with a frequency range of 10\n5 Hz to 10 −1 Hz.","source_sha256":"737246abfae47db049b2df1fb89d8f7f5a03b160d6c2f1fe70ed41145d8b7d18"},{"char_end":159,"char_start":34,"chunk_id":"mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88","document_char_end":62585,"document_char_start":62460,"evidence_id":"ev_f416168ef596716b","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"A 5 mm diameter rotating disk electrode (E5 RDE, PINE) was used to evaluate the electrocatalytic properties of the catalysts.","source_sha256":"33b392f70dfba85ad8230de078914f0f800ea81bab868ab68c7f02d4539ed326"},{"char_end":422,"char_start":314,"chunk_id":"mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88","document_char_end":62848,"document_char_start":62740,"evidence_id":"ev_d5dd2960587b06dc","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"To prepare the catalyst ink, 10 mg of catalyst powder and 2 mg of acetylene black were mixed in a container.","source_sha256":"33b392f70dfba85ad8230de078914f0f800ea81bab868ab68c7f02d4539ed326"},{"char_end":714,"char_start":582,"chunk_id":"mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88","document_char_end":63140,"document_char_start":63008,"evidence_id":"ev_dda57d59d344f7a2","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The mixture was sonicated in an ice bath for more than 2 h to ensure even mixing and dispersion of the catalyst and acetylene black.","source_sha256":"33b392f70dfba85ad8230de078914f0f800ea81bab868ab68c7f02d4539ed326"},{"char_end":796,"char_start":715,"chunk_id":"mdchk_ebc9d9fe4d67bc88","document_char_end":63222,"document_char_start":63141,"evidence_id":"ev_6952